--verification-cache stores its blobs compressed with zlib, from .NET's built-in System.IO.Compression, keeping a blob uncompressed only when compression would not make it smaller. Blob addresses and cache keys are still the SHA-256 of the uncompressed bytes, so they do not depend on the compression level or the library. A cache written by an earlier version still reads, and a corrupt or truncated compressed blob is a cache miss. See https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/388.
